      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "number",
                "French"
              ],
              "textCols": [
                0
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "0",
                  "zéro"
                ],
                [
                  "1, 2, 3",
                  "un, deux, trois"
                ],
                [
                  "4, 5, 6",
                  "quatre, cinq, six"
                ],
                [
                  "7, 8, 9",
                  "sept, huit, neuf"
                ],
                [
                  "10, 11, 12",
                  "dix, onze, douze"
                ],
                [
                  "13, 14, 15",
                  "treize, quatorze, quinze"
                ],
                [
                  "16",
                  "seize"
                ],
                [
                  "17, 18, 19",
                  "dix-sept, dix-huit, dix-neuf"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "You learn the numbers up to 16 by heart. From 17 they are built up: *dix-sept* = ten and seven."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Tens",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "number",
                "French"
              ],
              "textCols": [
                0
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "20",
                  "vingt"
                ],
                [
                  "30",
                  "trente"
                ],
                [
                  "40",
                  "quarante"
                ],
                [
                  "50",
                  "cinquante"
                ],
                [
                  "60",
                  "soixante"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "A hyphen is written between tens and units: *vingt-deux, trente-cinq*. Only *one* takes *et*: *vingt et un, trente et un*."
            },
            {
              "type": "compare",
              "items": [
                {
                  "en": "21",
                  "wrong": "vingt-un",
                  "fr": "vingt [[et]] un"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Un and une, pronunciation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*Un* becomes *une* in the feminine: *vingt et une filles*. The other numbers do not change."
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "en": "*Six* and *dix* before a consonant are read without the final sound (*six livres*), at the end of a sentence the *x* is read as s (*j'en ai six*). *Vingt* is read without the *t*, but *vingt-deux* with it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "J'ai quatorze ans.",
                  "en": "I'm fourteen."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il y a vingt-huit élèves dans ma classe.",
                  "en": "There are twenty-eight pupils in my class."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Mon père a quarante-trois ans.",
                  "en": "My father is forty-three."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "J'habite au numéro trente et un.",
                  "en": "I live at number thirty-one."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
