                  "un million"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Spelling",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "*Cent* takes an *-s* only in **round** hundreds: *deux cents*, but *deux cent dix*. *Mille* **never changes**: *trois mille*. *Million* is a noun: *deux millions de personnes*."
            },
            {
              "type": "compare",
              "items": [
                {
                  "en": "3,000",
                  "wrong": "trois milles",
                  "fr": "trois [[mille]]"
                },
                {
                  "en": "a hundred euros",
                  "wrong": "un cent euros",
                  "fr": "[[cent]] euros",
                  "note": "You don't say *un* before *cent* and *mille*."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Prices and years",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "A decimal comma is not read out in prices, you simply say two numbers. Thousands are separated by a space: *1 500 CZK*. Years are read as ordinary numbers: *1989* = *mille neuf cent quatre-vingt-neuf*."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "written",
                "said"
              ],
              "textCols": [
                0
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "2,99 €",
                  "deux euros quatre-vingt-dix-neuf"
                ],
                [
                  "15 €",
                  "quinze euros"
                ],
                [
                  "1 200 CZK",
                  "mille deux cents couronnes"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Ça coûte combien ? Douze euros cinquante.",
                  "en": "How much is it? Twelve euros fifty."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il y a deux cents élèves dans mon collège.",
                  "en": "There are two hundred pupils in my school."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Paris a plus de deux millions d'habitants.",
                  "en": "Paris has more than two million inhabitants."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Mon père est né en mille neuf cent quatre-vingt-cinq.",
                  "en": "My father was born in 1985."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
