    {
      "id": "numbers-more",
      "title": "More numbers: decimals, fractions, percentages, approximations",
      "fr": "les nombres (suite)",
      "level": "A2",
      "levelTo": "B1",
      "keywords": [
        "decimals",
        "virgule",
        "fractions",
        "la moitié",
        "un tiers",
        "un quart",
        "pourcentage",
        "pour cent",
        "environ",
        "une dizaine",
        "une centaine",
        "des milliers",
        "plus et moins",
        "arithmetic",
        "calcul",
        "mesures",
        "mètre",
        "kilo",
        "degrés"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "see": [
        "numbers-70-100",
        "big-numbers",
        "ordinals",
        "quantities"
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "In short",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "French writes **decimals with a comma** (*3,5* = *trois virgule cinq*) and **thousands with a space** (*10 000*). Fractions, percentages and approximate numbers use special words: *la moitié, un tiers, un quart, pour cent, une dizaine, une centaine*."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "type",
                "example",
                "reading"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "decimal",
                  "3,5",
                  "trois virgule cinq"
                ],
                [
                  "thousands",
                  "12 500",
                  "douze mille cinq cents"
                ],
                [
                  "half",
                  "1/2",
                  "la moitié, un demi"
                ],
                [
                  "third, quarter",
                  "1/3, 1/4",
                  "un tiers, un quart"
                ],
                [
                  "other fractions",
                  "2/5, 3/4",
                  "deux cinquièmes, trois quarts"
                ],
                [
                  "percentage",
                  "25 %",
                  "vingt-cinq pour cent"
                ],
                [
                  "approximate",
                  "~10, ~100",
                  "une dizaine, une centaine"
                ]
              ],
              "textCols": [
                0
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Approximate numbers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "The **-aine** nouns mean *about*: **une dizaine** (about 10), **une quinzaine** (about 15 or two weeks), **une vingtaine**, **une trentaine**, **une centaine** (about 100). **Des milliers** = thousands, **des millions** = millions. Add **de + noun**: *une dizaine de personnes*."
            },
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Il y a une vingtaine d'élèves.",
                  "en": "There are about twenty pupils."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Nous avons attendu une quinzaine de minutes.",
                  "en": "We waited about fifteen minutes."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Des milliers de personnes sont venues.",
                  "en": "Thousands of people came."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Le trajet dure environ deux heures.",
                  "en": "The journey takes about two hours."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Calculating",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "head": [
                "operation",
                "French",
                "example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "+",
                  "et / plus",
                  "Deux plus deux font quatre."
                ],
                [
                  "−",
                  "moins",
                  "Dix moins trois font sept."
                ],
                [
                  "×",
                  "fois",
                  "Trois fois quatre font douze."
                ],
                [
                  "÷",
                  "divisé par",
                  "Douze divisé par trois font quatre."
                ],
                [
                  "=",
                  "font / égale",
                  "Deux et deux font quatre."
                ]
              ],
              "textCols": [
                0
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "en": "The verb after the numbers is **font** (plural): *deux plus deux font quatre*."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Measures",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Height and size use **mesurer** or **faire**: *Il mesure un mètre quatre-vingts. Il fait 1,80 m.* Weight uses **peser**: *Elle pèse cinquante kilos.* Temperature uses **faire**: *Il fait vingt degrés.* Distance: *à dix kilomètres d'ici.* Speed: *cent kilomètres à l'heure.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Il mesure un mètre soixante-quinze.",
                  "en": "He is 1.75 m tall."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Ma valise pèse vingt kilos.",
                  "en": "My suitcase weighs 20 kilos."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "La ville est à trente kilomètres d'ici.",
                  "en": "The town is 30 km from here."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Il roule à cent trente kilomètres à l'heure.",
                  "en": "He drives at 130 km/h."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examples",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Mon frère a deux ans et demi.",
                  "en": "My brother is two and a half."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Quarante pour cent des élèves sont des filles.",
                  "en": "Forty per cent of the pupils are girls."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "J'ai payé la moitié du prix.",
                  "en": "I paid half the price."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Un quart d'heure, c'est quinze minutes.",
                  "en": "A quarter of an hour is fifteen minutes."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
